  "id": "COMPOUND:31188 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Mammeisin is implicated in the regulation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of target relationships that involve HL-60 cells. The evidence suggests that Mammeisin acts as a target of HL-60 cells, which in turn are targets of other compounds such as (-)-Licarin B, Centaurein, and Sagittasine C. These compounds all direct their targets to M-phase phosphoprotein 8, indicating a potential pathway where Mammeisin may influence the expression or activity of this protein through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The consistent presence of HL-60 as a common target in all three paths suggests a shared mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of cell cycle regulation. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Mammeisin in the regulation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, likely through the activation of pathways that are central to cell cycle control.",
